# Return the Favor with both modes (spree, CR 702.172): on its turn Bot2 casts an Ornithopter and, holding priority, a
# Lightning Bolt at Bot1. Bot1 answers with Return the Favor for {R}{R}{1}{1} (Black Lotus and Mox Ruby). Neither mode may
# target the Ornithopter: it is a creature spell (not "instant spell, sorcery spell"), and it has no target (not "with a
# single target"). Both target the Bolt. In the order written: the first copies it, the copy given Bot2 as its new target
# (CR 707.10c); the second changes the Bolt's own target to Bot2, the only other legal one, so nothing is asked (CR
# 115.7a). Bot2 takes both, 6; Bot1 none.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Return the Favor
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Ornithopter
Swamp x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Return the Favor.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Copy target; Change the target)
! Bot1.Target(Stack.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Stack.Lightning Bolt)
! Bot1.Target(Stack.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Stack.Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 14
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Ornithopter
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Stack.Count = 0
